  "query_preview": "..\nToday: A strengthening ridge over Central US will cause the \ntrough to retract north and push yesterdays system northeast \ninto lower Alberta and Western MT. Weak instability is still \nexpected over the higher terrain with 100-400 J/kg of Cape. \nEnsembles continue to have thunderstorm probabilities of 10-30 \npercent over the Cascades and mountains of the Idaho Panhandle. \nArea coverage will much less than Wednesday. With less moisture\nin the air on Thursday, it decreases the heavy downpour threat.\nMain concerns with the storms will be new fire starts and gusty\noutflow winds impacting ongoing and new fires. Highs will be a \nfew degrees cooler than Wednesday with a range of 70s to low \n80s.\n\nFriday through Wednesday: Friday will have some lingering mountain \nshowers as the trough is pushed out of the region by a strengthening \nridge. The region will be on the up slope side of the ridge, \nallowing for warmer, less dry air to infiltrate the region. \nUnfortunately, the pattern is not bringing widespread beneficial \nprecip to the region. Models are only giving brief periods of \nafternoon showers mainly over the higher terrains. The amounts are \nnot expected to be more than a tenth. Highs will continue to be in \nthe upper 80s and 90s. Overnight lows will be in the upper 40s to \nlow 60s. /JDC",
